[COMMENTS]
STATION,A velocity area station on the Bannock Burn which joins the River Forth downstream. GENERAL: Velocity area station. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10). STATION HYDROMETRY: Gabion river control initially showed signs of instability, but is now stable. The river flows through a large culvert style bridge downstream of the station and this may be an influential control feature during the largest floods. Both banks along the station consist of intermittent stretches of artificial vertical stone wall. The banks in 2019 are densely vegetated with tree branches growing over the channel. Pictures from the 1970s show that vegetation on the banks was much less during the earlier period of record. Two peak flow ratings across period of record. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11). FLOW REGIME: Small reservoirs in catchment have a slight effect on otherwise natural flows.
CATCHMENT,Mostly low-lying catchment. Bedrock mixed permeability; ~85% overlain by superficial deposits. Catchment is mostly moorland; some forest and arable landuse.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Although not gauged to AMAX 3, the vertical channel banks give some confidence in the extrapolation of the rating above the highest gauging.
[END]
